# User-visible text check (jargon_guard.py): accepted exceptions, each with its reason.

# Stored option codes (list/group_by/kanban); records are written by the list view
# switcher, never edited by hand, and es.po translates each code.
crm/fcrm/doctype/crm_view_settings/crm_view_settings.json
# Stored option code unlinked_orphan written by the product reconcile job; es.po
# translates it as «Sin ligar». Renaming it would need a data migration.
crm/fcrm/doctype/crm_product_sync_issue/crm_product_sync_issue.json

# Email template example: {{ lead_name }} and {{ grand_total }} are the placeholders
# the user types into a template.
msg::<p>Dear {{ lead_name }},</p>\n\n<p>This is a reminder for the payment of {{ grand_total }}.</p>\n\n<p>Thanks,</p>\n<p>Frappé</p>
# Frappe Cloud login only shows on sites hosted on Frappe Cloud (window.is_fc_site).
msg::Login to Frappe Cloud?
msg::Are you sure you want to login to your Frappe Cloud dashboard?
# Frappe Mail is the name of an email provider the admin picks, like Gmail.
msg::Frappe Mail Site

# Form Scripts editor (developers write the class there): the field name
# «trigger» clashes with the script's own trigger() method; the word is literal.
msg::⚠️ Avoid using "trigger" as a field name — it conflicts with the built-in trigger() method.

# n8n / automation connections: System Manager setup screens and API errors for whoever
# builds the automation. «webhook», «payload» and «message_id» are the words n8n itself uses
# for what they must paste or send; the payload is shown so the admin can see what was sent.
crm/fcrm/doctype/crm_integration/*
crm/fcrm/doctype/crm_integration_delivery/*
crm/integrations/webhooks.py
crm/integrations/channel.py
crm/api/integration.py
# API channel messages are never opened in Desk (no read permission); the notes say who writes them.
crm/fcrm/doctype/crm_channel_message/*::rule=written-by note
# The same n8n setup and API texts in the Spanish catalogue (crm/locale/es.po).
msg::Enter the full webhook URL, for example https://n8n.example.com/webhook/…
msg::Add the webhook URL from your n8n Webhook node first.
msg::Send message_id: your channel's own id for this message (up to 140 characters).
msg::message_id {0} was already used for a different text.
msg::Deliveries are written by the integration engine.
msg::Your webhook answered {0}. You can enable the connection now.
msg::Payload
# n8n's own names on the Automations (n8n) setup screens: its «Webhook» node, the URL the admin
# copies from it, and the Standard Webhooks «webhook-signature» header they check in n8n.
msg::1. Webhook URL
msg::Your n8n Webhook node's production URL. It must start with https://; for an n8n on your own network, ask support to allow its address.
msg::Use an https:// webhook URL. For an n8n on your own network, ask support to allow its address.
msg::Every event is signed (Standard Webhooks). Check the webhook-signature header in n8n with this secret to accept only events from this CRM.
msg::A connection sends signed events to an n8n Webhook node, and gives n8n an API key to answer customers, update records or ask the assistant.
